Now, by inserting prices $\tau_n\rightarrow 1$, into our CDF $F(x)=(c+1)x-cx^2$, and by expanding terms, we get the following inequality, for all $n>1$,
\begin{align}\label{eq:c}
(F_n)^n&=(c+1)^n(\tau_n)^n-(c+1)^{n-1}(\tau_n)^{n-1}c(\tau_n)^2+\cdots\\
&\ge (c+1)^{n-1}(\tau_n)^{n-1}\left((c+1)\tau_n-c(\tau_n)^{2}\right)\label{eq:20}
\end{align}
